  "query_preview": ".. High pressure builds back in across the Midwest\nThursday evening, lasting through at least the middle of next week.\nOnly exception will be a 20 to 40% chance for rain on Saturday. \nOtherwise, main forecast concerns for the extended center around\nfrost/freeze potential toward the end of the week as high sits\noverhead and 850 mb temperatures fall to near 0C. There will be a\nhigher likelihood of patchy frost occurrence several times across\nthe north through early next week, though we could be looking at a\nmore widespread frost/freeze event Sunday into Monday. Will \ncontinue to monitor trends for headline potential as we approach \nthe end of the growing season.",
